Cost of revenue consisted of the following for the periods presented (in thousands):

The increase in cost of revenue during the three months ended March 31, 2026, as compared to the same period in 2025, was primarily due to:

• co-location costs and depreciation of network equipment as a result of investment in our network, particularly as we build out our platform, including to support cloud infrastructure services and AI applications, to support future growth and scalability;

• network build-out and supporting services, particularly due to partner costs as we expand our compute partner program;

• payroll and related costs as a result of headcount growth to support our operations and the impact of the prior year
